01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Backbeat is a 1994 British biographical drama film directed and
co-written by Iain Softley in his feature directorial debut.

12
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
It chronicles the early days of the Beatles in Hamburg, West Germany, focusing primarily on the relationship between Stuart Sutcliffe
(Stephen Dorff) and John Lennon (Ian Hart), and also with Sutcliffe's German girlfriend Astrid Kirchherr (Sheryl Lee).

13
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
The film was produced by Channel Four Films and PolyGram Filmed
Entertainment, and was released in the UK on 1 April 1994.

14
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
It received mixed-to-positive reviews from critics, though was
well-received by the real-life Beatles and Kirchherr.

15
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The score by Don Was earned a BAFTA Award for Best Original Music, and the
film was nominated for Outstanding British Film and Best Sound.

